  "system": {
    "description": {
      "value": "<p><em>Overlay (midi-qol):</em> the Monster Manual's Engulf (Gelatinous Cube, Shambling Mound). A creature that fails the save is inside the engulfer: its token sits in the engulfer's space and moves with it, and it takes the engulfing damage each turn (the Gelatinous Cube's at the start of its turns, 3d6 acid; the Shambling Mound's at the start of the engulfed creature's turns). The engulfed creature can take an action to escape (its card at the start of its turn): the Gelatinous Cube's Strength (Athletics) check against its DC, the Shambling Mound's grapple (Athletics or Acrobatics against its passive Athletics); on a success it comes out on the nearest free space. The Gelatinous Cube engulfs as it moves: when its move enters a creature's space, its owner is asked whether it engulfs that creature, which then makes the save (once per move); on a success it moves to a free space beside the cube. Only a creature that fits the room left inside it (one Large, or up to four Medium or Small) is engulfed. A creature within 5 feet of the cube can pull an engulfed creature out as its action (DC 12 Strength (Athletics); the puller takes the Ooze Cube's acid damage).</p>",
      "chatFlavor": ""
    },
